  "status_text": "A million switches sit on a ring. Just 63 layers of gates are enough to tell whether all their rules can hold at once. Each position has its own table listing the allowed settings of that switch and the next two, wrapping around the ring. Give those tables to the circuit. It answers yes exactly when some setting works around the whole ring. Lean checked that the same wiring works for every choice of tables, using at most 384,000,003 AND and OR gates with at most two inputs each (L-clb-059).",
